---
source: crates/surfaces/cli/src/main.rs
expression: command.clone().render_long_help().to_string()
---
SpecForge compiler

Usage: specforge <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init          Initialize a new SpecForge project
  check         Validate .spec files and report diagnostics
  export        Export spec graph to stdout in various formats
  schema        Output the Graph Protocol schema
  model         Render the logical data model (entity kinds, fields, relationships)
  outline       Render the extension architecture (dependencies, enhancements, contributions)
  query         Query the graph at multiple resolutions
  trace         Show traceability chain for an entity, or for every entity
  format        Format .spec files
  stats         Show project statistics
  explore       Where to start reading the graph: starting points, hubs and unconnected entities
  review        Coverage gaps around an entity, or of the whole project
  infer-guide   What to look for in code to write a kind's entities
  add           Install an extension
  remove        Remove an installed extension
  extensions    List installed extensions
  publish       Publish an extension to the registry that serves its name: its binary, and the declaration read from it as the package's manifest
  search        Search for extensions in registries
  analyze       Run static analysis passes over the compiled project
  watch         Watch a project and rebuild incrementally on changes
  update        Update installed extensions to latest compatible versions
  login         Authenticate with a registry
  logout        Remove registry credentials
  providers     List configured providers
  collect       Run the project's test runners and record which entities their tests prove
  doctor        Run health checks on installed extensions
  mcp           Start MCP server (JSON-RPC over stdio)
  migrate       Migrate .spec files to the current format: the version header, a title for every block that has none, and the reference lists a file's blocks repeat moved into its `defaults`
  completions   Generate shell completions: the built-in commands, and the commands of the extensions the project at --path enables
  explain       Explain a diagnostic code
  infer-status  Show inference progress (analyzed files, gaps, stale entries)
  extension     Extension authoring commands
  help          Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version

Extensions add commands: specforge <extension> <command>, e.g. `specforge product features`.
`specforge <extension> --help` lists an extension's commands.
